{
  "name": "Ender Cell",
  "icon": "powah:ender_cell_starter",
  "category": "storage_transfer",
  "sortnum": 2,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Ender Cells are endpoints for a wireless FE pool identified by owner + channel."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Two Ender Cells on the same owner/channel see the same stored energy even when they are far apart."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "$(bold)Important: a new channel has no useful storage until you add capacity.$()"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Select the channel, then Shift-click a Battery or Energy Cell into the Ender Cell GUI. The item is consumed and its capacity is permanently added to that channel."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If the consumed Battery or Energy Cell already contains FE, that energy is imported too."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This is why there is no normal persistent “capacity slot”: the extender is an upgrade consumed into the network."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "$(bold)Endpoint transfer (FE/t)$()$(br)Starter: 1k$(br)Basic: 4k$(br)Hardened: 10k$(br)Blazing: 40k"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "$(bold)Endpoint transfer (FE/t)$()$(br)Niotic: 100k$(br)Spirited: 400k$(br)Nitro: 2M"
    },
    {
